status: reject_clean
exit: 1
match: place sections are immutable
note: |
  Form `x.f = e`: mutating a place field. Place sections are immutable in 1.0;
  mutation goes through Space cells (`x = e` on a `be`-bound local) or a fresh
  `new`. Until 2026-07-02 this CRASHED the compiler (an uncaught exception in
  emit_mlir, `__space_update_here` had no lowering); now it is rejected cleanly at
  type-check. This fixture pins that it stays a clean rejection, never a crash again.
